WEBVTT

00:00:09.925 --> 00:00:11.485
No more bets, please.

00:00:11.565 --> 00:00:13.125
Come on, fuzzy dice!

00:00:13.245 --> 00:00:15.205
-Number four. Easy four.
-Yeah!

00:00:15.245 --> 00:00:17.245
Air freshener. Antenna balls.

00:00:17.285 --> 00:00:19.085
Spark-a plugs.

00:00:19.205 --> 00:00:21.605
This place looks like
it's made outta gold!

00:00:21.685 --> 00:00:24.925
HOLLEY: That's because it is.
Now, be careful what you say.

00:00:25.085 --> 00:00:27.045
MATER: Why is that?

00:00:27.085 --> 00:00:29.085
What do you mean, "Don't talk to ya"?

00:00:29.125 --> 00:00:31.565
You want me to stop talkin' to ya
right now?

00:00:31.645 --> 00:00:33.085
You are acting strange today, Ivan.

00:00:34.405 --> 00:00:37.285
I have no idea
what you're talking about,

00:00:37.365 --> 00:00:40.605
"Alexander Hugo, aka Chop Shop Alex."

00:00:40.685 --> 00:00:42.645
You got a lot of aka's, Alex.

00:00:42.725 --> 00:00:46.765
But that makes sense, seein's how
you's wanted in France, Germany...

00:00:46.885 --> 00:00:48.845
Mater, stop it!

00:00:48.925 --> 00:00:50.285
OK, OK, keep your voice down!

00:00:50.325 --> 00:00:52.285
You gonna make me arrested!

00:00:52.365 --> 00:00:54.925
Don't mess with Ivan today.
He's in a bad mood.

00:00:54.965 --> 00:00:56.725
He's so good!

00:00:58.245 --> 00:01:00.005
Victor!

00:01:00.645 --> 00:01:01.645
Hey, Victor!

00:01:02.965 --> 00:01:04.485
-There you are!
-Come in!

00:01:04.565 --> 00:01:08.725
Victor Hugo, I'm J Curby Gremlin.
From Detroit.

00:01:08.805 --> 00:01:10.565
It's good to see you.

00:01:10.645 --> 00:01:12.525
Is the big boss here yet?

00:01:12.605 --> 00:01:15.725
-No, not yet.
-He's supposed to be here any minute.

00:01:15.805 --> 00:01:17.565
(KNOCKING)

00:01:17.645 --> 00:01:19.525
(HORN BEEPS, KNOCKING)

00:01:19.605 --> 00:01:21.605
Here we go.

00:01:23.885 --> 00:01:25.325
Guten Tag.

00:01:25.365 --> 00:01:27.365
It's just the professor.

00:01:27.485 --> 00:01:29.125
Zündapp! When is he coming?

00:01:29.165 --> 00:01:31.165
He's already here.

00:01:33.125 --> 00:01:35.485
(DISGUISED VOICE)
Welcome, everyone.

00:01:35.565 --> 00:01:38.845
I wish I could be with you
on this very special day,

00:01:38.925 --> 00:01:40.965
but my clutch assembly broke.

00:01:41.005 --> 00:01:43.165
-You know how it is.
-Forget about it.

00:01:43.205 --> 00:01:44.885
We know how you feel.

00:01:44.965 --> 00:01:47.165
-Descramble that voice.
-I'm trying.

00:01:47.205 --> 00:01:49.325
Oh, it's too sophisticated.

00:01:49.445 --> 00:01:51.445
We are here to celebrate.

00:01:51.965 --> 00:01:53.965
Today, all your hard work pays off.

00:01:55.005 --> 00:01:57.765
The world turned their backs
on cars like us.

00:01:57.845 --> 00:02:01.325
They stopped manufacturing us,
stopped making our parts.

00:02:01.365 --> 00:02:05.885
The only thing they haven't stopped
doing is laughing at us.

00:02:06.565 --> 00:02:10.925
They've called us terrible names:
jalopy, rust bucket, heap,

00:02:11.445 --> 00:02:15.205
clunker, junker, beater,
wreck, rattletrap,

00:02:16.525 --> 00:02:17.845
lemon.

00:02:17.925 --> 00:02:20.205
But their insults just give us strength.

00:02:21.565 --> 00:02:26.565
Because today, my friends,
that all ends!

00:02:27.725 --> 00:02:29.845
DARRELL: There's smoke
on the casino bridge!

00:02:29.925 --> 00:02:30.965
Oh, no!

00:02:31.045 --> 00:02:32.645
It's Carla Veloso, the Brazilian race car!

00:02:37.645 --> 00:02:39.565
-What just happened?
-I'm working on it.

00:02:39.605 --> 00:02:41.405
(CHEERING)

00:02:41.685 --> 00:02:45.405
They laughed at us,
but now it's our turn to laugh back.

00:02:47.605 --> 00:02:50.645
DAVID: Another crash!
It's number 9, Nigel Gearsley.

00:02:51.285 --> 00:02:53.045
Embrace your inner lemon.

00:02:53.085 --> 00:02:54.765
Let it drive you.

00:02:54.845 --> 00:02:58.245
I'm detecting an extremely strong
electromagnetic pulse.

00:03:02.205 --> 00:03:04.085
-Finn, it's the camera.
-Where?

00:03:04.205 --> 00:03:05.965
On the tower!

00:03:08.365 --> 00:03:12.445
LEMON KINGPIN: This was meant to
be alternative fuel's greatest moment.

00:03:12.525 --> 00:03:16.405
But after today,
everyone will race back to gasoline.

00:03:16.445 --> 00:03:21.445
And we, the owners of the world's
largest untapped oil reserve

00:03:21.525 --> 00:03:23.765
will become the most powerful cars
in the world!

00:03:24.285 --> 00:03:25.765
Get out of the way!

00:03:25.845 --> 00:03:27.445
(SPEAKS ITALIAN)

00:03:52.085 --> 00:03:53.725
(SHOUTING IN ITALIAN)

00:04:00.965 --> 00:04:05.205
They will come to us, and they will have
no choice, because they will need us.

00:04:12.365 --> 00:04:13.725
Huh? Whoa!

00:04:14.565 --> 00:04:16.565
We figured you might stop by!

00:04:19.325 --> 00:04:21.965
LEMON KINGPIN:
And they will finally respect us!

00:04:22.045 --> 00:04:24.045
So hold your hoods high!

00:04:24.325 --> 00:04:27.365
After today, you will never again
be ashamed of who you are!

00:04:28.805 --> 00:04:30.525
No!

00:04:30.605 --> 00:04:33.525
Long live lemons!

00:04:33.565 --> 00:04:35.925
BRENT: Number 7 is loose!
Shu Todoroki!

00:04:59.885 --> 00:05:01.165
Finn?

00:05:02.005 --> 00:05:04.605
BRENT: Bumper to bumper
as they approach the finish line!

00:05:04.725 --> 00:05:06.645
McQueen's the winner!
Francesco's second!

00:05:06.725 --> 00:05:09.165
They have no idea
what happened behind them.

00:05:09.205 --> 00:05:10.725
This is impossible!

00:05:10.805 --> 00:05:12.725
That's what I'm talking about! Ka-chow!

00:05:12.805 --> 00:05:14.605
-(SIRENS BLARE)
-What happened?

00:05:14.725 --> 00:05:17.405
-Where are all the other cars?
-What is going on?

00:05:18.205 --> 00:05:19.405
Oh, no!

00:05:25.405 --> 00:05:29.005
Sir Axlerod, is the final race in London
still going to take place?

00:05:29.125 --> 00:05:31.085
I suppose that...

00:05:31.165 --> 00:05:34.405
(SIGHS) The show must go on,
as they say.

00:05:34.525 --> 00:05:36.565
I can't believe this is really happening!

00:05:36.645 --> 00:05:37.805
Quiet!

00:05:37.885 --> 00:05:40.965
Will you require all the racers
to still run on allinol?

00:05:41.045 --> 00:05:45.885
I cannot, in good conscience, continue
to risk the lives of any more race cars.

00:05:46.445 --> 00:05:50.285
The final race will not be run on allinol.

00:05:50.365 --> 00:05:53.085
There you have it, a clearly devastated
Sir Miles Axlerod

00:05:53.125 --> 00:05:57.245
announcing that he will not require
the cars to use allinol for the final race.

00:05:57.445 --> 00:05:58.765
A toast!

00:05:58.805 --> 00:06:02.485
To the death of allinol
and alternative fuel forever!

00:06:02.605 --> 00:06:05.445
Mater, abort the mission.

00:06:05.565 --> 00:06:08.925
They've got Finn. Get out of there.
Get out of there right now.

00:06:09.685 --> 00:06:11.445
How is your grandfather?

00:06:11.485 --> 00:06:13.445
(CHANTING) Long live lemons!

00:06:13.565 --> 00:06:15.885
Isn't this a great party, Ivan, huh?

00:06:16.005 --> 00:06:17.765
Oh, yeah, it's unbelievable.

00:06:17.885 --> 00:06:19.965
You are not leaving, are you?

00:06:20.045 --> 00:06:22.005
Uh...of course I ain't leaving.

00:06:22.085 --> 00:06:23.845
-McQUEEN ON TV: I'm just in shock...
-McQueen?

00:06:24.685 --> 00:06:26.605
Crashes are a part of racing, I know,

00:06:26.725 --> 00:06:29.965
but something like that
should never happen.

00:06:30.005 --> 00:06:33.565
DARRELL: You can choose your fuel
for the final race. What it'll be?

00:06:33.645 --> 00:06:35.125
-Allinol.
-(ASTONISHED GASPS)

00:06:35.205 --> 00:06:36.485
DARRELL: After today?

00:06:36.605 --> 00:06:39.525
My friend Fillmore says it's safe.
That's good enough for me.

00:06:39.645 --> 00:06:42.005
I didn't stand by a friend of mine
recently.

00:06:42.085 --> 00:06:44.325
I'm not gonna make
the same mistake twice.

00:06:44.445 --> 00:06:47.325
So a surprising revelation
from Lightning McQueen.

00:06:47.485 --> 00:06:51.085
He will use allinol in the final race,
despite what occurred today.

00:06:51.205 --> 00:06:53.885
-..till Lightning McQueen is dead.
-Of course.

00:06:54.885 --> 00:06:58.125
Allinol must be finished for good.

00:06:58.725 --> 00:07:01.165
McQueen cannot win the last race.

00:07:01.885 --> 00:07:04.165
Lightning McQueen must be killed!

00:07:04.245 --> 00:07:05.485
No!

00:07:06.205 --> 00:07:08.525
(HORN PLAYS LA CUCARACHA)

00:07:12.645 --> 00:07:14.525
It's the American spy!

00:07:15.965 --> 00:07:17.085
Dad-gum!

00:07:17.165 --> 00:07:19.245
COMPUTER: Gatling gun.
Request acknowledged.

00:07:19.325 --> 00:07:21.325
ZÜNDAPP: Down! Everybody, down!

00:07:21.325 --> 00:07:24.285
-Shoot! I didn't mean...
-COMPUTER: Request acknowledged.

